  "goodToKnow": "Der Discounter is a discount supermarket, a German invention exported worldwide: Aldi (split into Aldi Nord and Aldi Süd, founded by the Albrecht brothers in Essen) and Lidl (Schwarz Group) are global giants, joined by Netto and Penny. They offer a limited range at low prices, while Vollsortimenter like Edeka and Rewe carry more. Germans spend a relatively small share of income on food. Plural: die Discounter."
